    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0670" n="1504" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/552</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-17T17:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 17, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.23 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3194. My 3189, June 16, 1 p.m., in regard to the Dutch East Indian convoy. The
                    French Minister without instructions from his Government has today addressed a
                    note to the Dutch Government asking whether it will give France the same
                    assurances that it has given Great Britain in answer to the British note of June
                    7 telegraphed you in my 3163, June 13, 4 p.m. He also asks what these assurances
                    are. He hopes to see Loudon tomorrow and get his answer.</p>
                <p>Do you wish me to take similar or other steps in the matter?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
